# Normally you do NOT hand-write this -- run new-workflow.sh and it generates
#   ~/.config/rocoto-systemd/<instance>.scrontab
# ready to paste into `scrontab -e`.  This file is the annotated reference.
#
# The watchdog:
#   - verifies user lingering (tries to enable it; fails loudly if it can't);
#   - verifies this is the pinned node (if PIN_NODE is set) and refuses otherwise;
#   - starts rocoto-workflow@<instance>.service if it died and the workflow
#     is not settled;
#   - once the workflow has NO Active cycles, stops the service and runs
#     `scancel` on itself.  Slurm then prepends "#DISABLED: " to the lines
#     below and no further cycle runs -- a clean, automatic shutdown.
#
# No '#SCRON --export=' here: on at least one Slurm/scrontab setup it was
# confirmed to NOT reach watchdog.sh's process environment at all on
# scrontab-triggered (re)executions -- every exported var missing, every
# tick, from install onward. Instead, watchdog.sh reads WF/DB/WD/PIN_NODE/the
# ROCOTO_* vars/the tunables from ~/.config/rocoto-systemd/<instance>.env,
# which new-workflow.sh writes BEFORE this job ever ticks.
# The only thing that has to reach the job itself is INSTANCE, passed below
# as a plain literal argument (not a variable -- nothing for scrontab to
# substitute or drop).
# PIN_NODE + --nodelist are present only when the instance is node-isolated.

#SCRON --partition=cron_c6
#SCRON --account=bil-fire2-oar
#SCRON --time=00:03:00
#SCRON --mem=2G
#SCRON --job-name=rocoto_wd_rrfsdet
#SCRON --dependency=singleton
#SCRON --nodelist=gaea61
#SCRON --output=/gpfs/f6/arfs-gsl/world-shared/gge/rrfs2/regressionTests/conus12km/exp/rrfsdet/logs/watchdog_rrfsdet.out

@hourly REPLACE_WITH_HOME/rocoto-systemd/watchdog.sh rrfsdet
